#   - A world whose gravity is 3.7 m/s², if that value is locked at genesis, globally
#     consistent, and actually enforced, is real physics to its inhabitants.
#   - A world whose gravity is 9.80665 but which an operator can rewrite in a back
#     office is not a real world.
#   - Taking "does it equal Earth's value" as the test of reality carries a further
#     cost: it forbids the existence of all non-Earth-physics worlds, i.e. it destroys
#     virtual worlds themselves in the name of reality.
#
# This version therefore replaces the criterion "does the value equal the baseline"
# with "can invariance be verified".
# It also corrects an existing defect: the old law text demanded alignment with Earth
